## Signature

- Provided by: **Claude Opus 5 (anthropic/claude-opus-5)** — 2026-10-08
- Method: fresh public internet research only. Research steps attempted and their outcomes: a direct fetch of `benchlm.ai/md/models/grok-5.md` (**404**, while sibling Grok entries resolve); a targeted search for `xAI "Grok 5" benchmark context window pricing release`, which returned **seven results, every one of which is a release-date-speculation article rather than a model page**; and a full read of ZBuild's guide, which was first published 2026-03-27, **rewritten because "most of the original predictions turned out wrong", and re-verified source-by-source on 2026-10-11** — it supplied the "has not been released as of October 11, 2026" determination, the explicit "architecture, context window, pricing, benchmarks, open-source status: not announced. Any numbers you see are guesses" statement, the full dated promise-versus-reality timeline from Musk's October 2025 AGI remark through his 2026-09-14 placement of Grok 4.8 and 4.9 ahead of Grok 5, the Polymarket pricing and the two contracts that resolved No, the 6T-versus-10T ambiguity, the Grok 4.6/4.7/4.8 parameter comparisons, the live API model list and prices, the Grok 4.7 specifications and CursorBench/Terminal-Bench figures, the 2026-05-15 retirement of Grok 4, Grok 4 Fast, Grok Code Fast 1 and Grok 3, the xAI → SpaceXAI → SpaceXSI corporate sequence, the Colossus 1 lease to Anthropic, and the Colossus 2 hardware and capacity claims including Tom's Hardware's contradicting satellite analysis. Corroborating negative evidence was taken from geotoolbox (2026-09-29, "isn't out yet"), felloai ("still training as of September 2026"), computeunion (2026-06-23, "no public API") and overchat (which labels the 6T / 1.5M-context / native-multimodal specs as "reportedly"). **The mutual contradiction among speculative context-window figures — 128K in this repo's placeholder, 1.5M at overchat, 2M at computeunion — is reported explicitly as evidence that nothing is known, rather than averaged into a number.** The repo's own `meta.json` was read only to identify what was being claimed and is reported as a placeholder. Grok 4.7's measured benchmarks are quoted **only** as context for what the shipping flagship does and were deliberately **not** imported as Grok 5 data; no data was imported from `grok-4`, `grok-4.1`, `grok-4.20`, `grok-4-fast` or `grok-build-0.1`, and no peer `model/` findings files were read. Unavailable items — every benchmark figure, the release date, the context window, the modalities, the pricing, the architecture and the model's existence as a released artefact — are recorded as "no verified public data found" rather than estimated.
- Future sources: add a new file next to this one, e.g. `GPT_5.md`, using the same headings.
